    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n52 Glasnevin Hill is an attractive three bedroom end of terrace home with side pedestrian access. Built in the early 1900's this home offers a wonderful opportunity to acquire a property full of character in a mature and well-established residential setting. \n \nThis home has been very well maintained by the current owners. The property is ready for its next chapter and will appeal to buyers looking to create a home tailored to their own tastes and requirements.\n \nExtending to approximately 116 sq m approx. The accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall with guest wc, storage, two spacious interconnecting reception rooms, both featuring open fireplaces, a breakfast room and kitchen to the rear. \nAt return level there is a generous bedroom and shower room. On the first floor, the large principal bedroom spans the full width of the property to the front, while a second double bedroom overlooks the rear garden.\nAnother feature of the home is the rear garden, which enjoys a south west facing orientation and can be accessed from the house or side entrance. \n \nThe property benefits from a convenient and well-established location with a wide range of amenities nearby, including local shops, cafés, restaurants, Griffith Park and the National Botanic Gardens. Dublin City University and St Patrick's Campus are within walking distance, while Trinity College Dublin and University College Dublin are easily accessible by public transport. A selection of well-regarded primary and secondary schools, along with local sports clubs such as Na Fianna GAA Club and Tolka Rovers, are also close by.\nThe area is well served by public transport, with regular bus routes and Drumcondra Train Station within walking distance. The M50, M1, Dublin City Centre, and Dublin Airport are also readily accessible."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.22m x 4.10m\nwith carpet flooring, understairs storage and guest wc.\n\nLiving Room - 3.70m x 3.90m\nspacious room to the front with carpet flooring, and original open fireplace. Interconnecting doors lead to the dining room.\n\nDining Room - 3.20m x 3.97m\nwith carpet flooring, original open fireplace.\n\nBreakfast Room - 3.00m x 3.80m\nspacious room with Stanley cooker and access to the rear garden.\n\nKitchen - 3.01m x 1.88m\nwith ample storage and plumbed for a washing machine and dish washer.\n\nBedroom One - 5.14m x 3.94m\nspanning the width of the house with 2 windows flooding the room with natural light and original fireplace.\n\nBedroom Two - 3.30m x 4.00m\nlarge double room with carpet flooring and original fireplace.\n\nReturn - \n\n\nBedroom Three - 2.90m x 2.50m\nlarge single room with carpet flooring.\n\nShower Room - 1.90m x 2.40m\npartly tiled with wc, whb and shower.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Gas heating </li><li>Side entrance </li><li>South west facing rear garden </li><li>Many original features </li><li>Excellent location close to abundance of amenities </li><li>Short drive to M1, M50 and Dublin Airport</ul>"
